{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1731 SUBAGENTS AS CHILD ROWS (lib/sessions/subagent.ts, trpc sessions.subagent; the device: crates/eagent's SubagentEdge → crates/coding). A CLI subagent (Claude's Task/Agent tool and its workflow agents, Codex's spawned threads) is a child `sessions` row the DEVICE writes with `device.subagent` {sessionId = its parent, deviceId, key = the CLI's own id of it, freshId, status running|ended, failed?, summary?; the server also takes title}. The first edge of a key under a parent writes the row: one below the parent (rootId inherited, depth + 1), the parent's team, member, visibility and device (the server: its repository, branch and worktree too, cli/account/model; never its own branch or PR), `subagentKey` = the key, running and busy at once with startedAt stamped: never queued or claimed, no brief, no first input, no card on the parent (the parent's transcript already shows the tool call; the row shows under its Sessions tab). A later `running` edge is progress (a resumed key that had ended is live again in place); every edge stamps lastActivityAt on the row AND its parent (a subagent working is a sign of life of its parent). `ended` ends it: its summary (dropped in a keyed tree, #FEED-192: the device sends none there; failed = copy.subagentFailed / subagentFailedBare) posts as its own last agent line (non-waking), then End as tree.json (session_ended on itself, its report to its WATCHERS) with NO kill (its process is its parent's). THE BUS NEVER POSTS A SUBAGENT'S LINE INTO ITS PARENT (no claim, turn, ask, wall or report: the parent is the CLI process that ran it and has it in-band), so a subagent never wakes its parent. An edge for an ended parent, or from a device the parent left, is ignored; a blank key = `invalid` (copy.subagentNoKey); an edge under a subagent = `invalid` (copy.subagentNoChildren; the CLI's subagents attach to the session that runs the CLI). CAPS: a subagent holds no live slot (rules.caps), is never refused by the depth cap, and is no sub-session for reuse.json's maxChildren; today's limits stay exactly as they are for every other row. MESSAGING: a subagent takes no input of its own (a message mid-run would resume a second copy of it, EXP-856): a send to one, running or ended, is the same send to its PARENT (live input, revive or continue, per tree.json), its result names the parent and carries copy.subagentRedirect as `warning`. send.start under a subagent = `invalid` (copy.subagentNoChildren). Linking issues to it is the server's and works as for any child. STRAYS: a parent whose turn is over (a report leaves it not busy: idle, a lost process, its end) runs no subagent any more: the live subagents its device never closed end then, oldest first, before the parent itself ends. The watchdog and the heartbeat's live list never look at a subagent (its liveness is its parent's). A person may End a subagent row (no kill).",
